    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1619">

                <pb facs="1320" n="1204" xml:id="pg1204"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.77/130.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-08-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 21, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am informed by Mr. J. M. Hyatt that in the contract referred to in my telegram
                    of yesterday the provision for hypothecating the $250,000 annuity has been
                    replaced by a provision for hypothecating a portion of the $6,000,000 belonging
                    to the Government of Panama in New York. Mr. Hyatt also says that the
                    substitution has been acquiesced in by the Department of State.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
